  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed and maximizing forward exploration. Recovery states are one-shot and only allow the safest action for the given obstacle. The design ensures no oscillation, no forward/random_walk in obstacle states, and quick return to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and sensor-driven transitions.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-maximizing action selection: forward/random_walk in clear, rotate or back out in obstacle, and quick recovery to exploration."
